DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ffww__uuppddaattee utility installs, updates, or deletes firmware for _d_r_i_v_e_r
     from the Internet.  By default, ffww__uuppddaattee tries to determine which
     firmware are needed.

     Since firmware with an acceptable license is already present in OpenBSD,
     ffww__uuppddaattee exists purely to deal with firmware that may not be freely dis‐
     tributed with OpenBSD.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa      Install or update firmware for all drivers.  It is an error to
             specify this option with any _d_r_i_v_e_r arguments.

     --dd      Delete firmware for _d_r_i_v_e_r.  If used without parameters, delete
             all firmware that is not required by a driver.  If used in con‐
             junction with --aa, delete firmware for all drivers.

     --DD _p_a_t_h
             Use the dmesg(8) output from _p_a_t_h rather than _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_d_m_e_s_g_._b_o_o_t
             to determine which firmware are needed.

     --FF      Download SHA256.sig and firmware .tgz to the current directory.

     --ll      List drivers without installing.  With --FF lists the full path to
             the files that will be downloaded.

     --nn      Dry run.  Do not actually install or update any firmware; just
             report the steps that would be taken.

     --pp _p_a_t_h
             Use _p_a_t_h, either a local directory or a URL, as the source for
             firmware instead of the default location.

     --vv      Turn on verbose output.  This flag can be specified multiple
             times for increased verbosity.

